        <mxCell id="otrade" value="KEY TRADE-OFFS&#10;&#10;• PostgreSQL (events) vs NoSQL: pick PG for PostGIS spatial + B-tree date idx + ACID booking txn. Give up: harder horizontal write-scale -&gt; mitigate with read replicas + per-event partition.&#10;• Elasticsearch (search reads) vs query PG directly: scalable geo/full-text at 50k QPS. Give up: eventual consistency via CDC (acceptable — browse need not be strongly consistent).&#10;• Redis locks vs DB row locks for reservation: Redis = fast, TTL auto-release, no long-held DB txn. Give up: a 2nd source of truth -&gt; PG conditional UPDATE remains the true arbiter; Redis is the optimistic fast-path.&#10;• Redis SET NX EX + Lua vs Redlock: single-shard atomic acquire is enough at one-event scale; Redlock only if locks span shards. Give up: cross-shard safety not needed.&#10;• Waiting room (virtual queue) vs just failing excess requests: protects booking service + fair ordering + good UX. Give up: extra infra + queue-wait latency.&#10;• Kafka for webhooks vs sync processing: durability, replay, decouples payment spikes. Give up: added eventual-consistency + ops." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=8;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1780" width="780" height="320" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="odeep" value="DEEP DIVES (specific to this system)&#10;&#10;1. ATOMIC RESERVATION: SET seat:{id} {userId} NX EX 600. value=userId so release is a Lua compare-and-delete (never delete another user's lock after your TTL lapses). Multi-seat (e.g. 4 adjacent): one Lua script checks ALL seats free then sets ALL — all-or-nothing, no stranded half-locks.&#10;&#10;2. OVERSELL RACE (TTL expiry vs late payment): make PG the arbiter. Confirm = UPDATE eventseat SET status=booked WHERE id=? AND status=reserved AND reserved_by=A. 0 rows -&gt; A lost it -&gt; auto-refund. Refund is the rare exception, not the mechanism.&#10;&#10;3. SCALE-BREAK (1-2M users / 50k seats): naive = every reserve hammers booking svc + Redis. Fix = Waiting Room (Redis ZSET / token bucket) admits N users/sec into a live seat-map session; queue throttles CONCURRENCY, not seat choice (seats chosen live from current availability).&#10;&#10;4. HOT KEY (reads): all hit GET /events/:id for one event -&gt; replicate that cache entry across Redis replicas, client fan-out. HOT PARTITION (writes): all bookings for one event hit same PG rows/shard -&gt; per-event partition / in-memory seat-map authority.&#10;&#10;5. OPERABILITY: alert on oversell count, reservation-success rate, lock-expiry-vs-payment races, queue depth &amp; wait-time SLA, Redis-node failover (lost locks). Consistency: strong on booking (PG txn), eventual on browse (ES/cache)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="860" y="1780" width="800" height="320" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
